      "id": "impl.safety-hardening",
      "stage": "implementation",
      "agent": "sdlc:implementer",
      "description": "Close two already-named open risks. (1) RateLimitingAdmissionControl's bucket map has no eviction (release-notes-1.1.0.md) -- replace the plain ConcurrentHashMap with a bounded, evicting cache (Caffeine: maximumSize + expireAfterAccess, e.g. 1 hour) so wide address scanning cannot grow it unbounded. Keep the same Bucket4j bucket logic; only the storage/eviction changes. (2) The request body is fully parsed by Jackson before @Size(max=8192) is checked (release-notes-1.0.0.md sec.review WARNING) -- add an earlier guard: either a Jackson2ObjectMapperBuilderCustomizer setting StreamReadConstraints.maxStringLength to a reasonable bound (e.g. 16384) in config/, or a Content-Length pre-check filter that rejects an oversized POST /api/links body with 413 before the body is read. Prefer the Jackson StreamReadConstraints approach -- simpler, no new filter, no interaction with SecurityHeadersFilter. Do not touch UrlValidator, RedirectController, or anything auth/expiry-related -- explicitly out of scope per this run's understanding.md.",
      "evidence": "mvn -q -DskipFrontend=true -DskipTests compile",
